+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"build","node_id":"F2","attempt":2,"source":"gate","source_ref":"gate.stub (ok:false) at 305789df2125abfa6ff2e8ba2b0aa9805789008c, docs/trace/build/F2/loop.jsonl:4","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"GET-1","layer":"api","files":["src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/PolicyMappings.cs","tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/RetrieveStatusTests.cs","tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/RetrieveCurrentTermTests.cs"],"root_cause":"Symptom: 5 RetrieveStatusTests rows pass on the stub (Policy_sold_to_start_today_reads_back_Active, Status_on_the_start_date_is_Active, Status_on_the_end_date_is_Active, Status_at_23_30_UTC_on_an_end_date_in_GMT_is_Active, Status_at_22_59_UTC_on_an_end_date_in_BST_is_Active). Cause: src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/PolicyMappings.cs:32 hard-codes the status as PolicyStatus.Active. Active is one of the three values the GET-1 tests expect (RetrieveStatusTests.cs:48, 62, 69, 84, 100 through PolicyResponseAssert.cs:30). Each of these one-term rows also expects currentTermNumber 1 (PolicyResponseAssert.cs:31), which the canned 1 at PolicyMappings.cs:33 matches too (see I2), so the status assertion is the only one that can fail them. The real value is already there: details.Status is computed by Policy.StatusOn(today) in PolicyService.cs:69-70, and the stub ignores it. The same canned Active also matches the status assertions at RetrieveCurrentTermTests.cs:39 and :49. That shared cause is one of the two reasons the first two current-term rows pass (I2 has the other). Fix direction: the canned status must be a value that no GET-1 test expects. The tests expect Pending, Active and Expired, so Cancelled is the only enum member they never expect.","fingerprint":"GET-1|src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/PolicyMappings.cs|canned-status-active-coincides","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the stub commit for t2 and the existing RetrieveStatusTests Active rows, When the orchestrator re-runs gate.stub (Api.Tests filtered by Rule=GE